+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `database` | A PostgreSQL connection with pgvector; start-up fails without it | None for migrations and vector operators, which run against the real server; a fake store for unit tests | Required | Drizzle over the host's connection | PostgreSQL 18 line; an extension upgrade is recorded in the release |
+| `object_storage` | Put, get, delete, list and short-lived signed URLs on a private bucket; reports off and unavailable | An in-memory object store under `tests/fakes/` | Conditional: the application stores files | `await host.storage.put(key, bytes, { contentType })` | The S3 API; the provider is recorded per deployment |
+| `embeddings` | Vectors for texts with the configured model and dimensions, never another length; reports off, missing credentials and unavailable | A deterministic fake embedder | Conditional: semantic retrieval is used | `const [vector] = await host.embeddings.embed([text])` | A model or dimension change is a re-embedding migration (rule 6) |
+| `vector_search` | Upsert, search and delete in the active index; permission filters applied before results leave; answers off when embeddings are off | An in-memory index | Conditional: semantic retrieval is used | `await host.vectors.search(text, { limit: 10, filter })` | Rebuildable from stored content; HNSW up to 2,000 dimensions (`vector`) or 4,000 (`halfvec`) |
