+## Host adapters for data, objects and embeddings
+
+The host's adapters over the application foundation stack (PRO current §W.6) are the supported
+implementations of four host capabilities: `database` (PostgreSQL with pgvector), `object_storage`
+(any S3-compatible provider), `embeddings` and `vector_search`. A module that needs one lists it in
+`dependencies.host` and uses that adapter. A module never carries its own database driver or engine
+(SQLite included), S3 client, embedding client or vector store, and never reads a credential from an
+env file. A receiving application binds the same four capabilities to its own host; the module's
+source and transfer plan never carry their configuration or credentials.
+
+A module that imports an S3 SDK, an embedding API client or a database driver directly needs an
+adapter before it is compatible; it is not a compatible capability. A module whose descriptor omits
+a host capability its code uses has an undeclared dependency. Tool follow-up: `modules.mjs plan`
+reports both; until it does, the integration review records them.
